.{
    // Repository-root Zig manifest so the package is consumable via the clean
    // `zig fetch --save <tag tarball>` + `dep.module("causalontology")` flow.
    // The library sources live under bindings/zig/src/; this root manifest
    // exposes the module, mirroring the root Package.swift (SwiftPM) and the
    // root composer.json (Packagist) — tag-based channels read the repo root.
    .name = "causalontology",
    .version = "4.0.0",
    .minimum_zig_version = "0.13.0",
    .dependencies = .{},
    // Zig's package manager PRUNES the downloaded tarball to exactly these
    // paths before hashing and caching it: whatever is missing here does not
    // exist for a consumer, however plainly it sits in the repository. This
    // list once held only build.zig, build.zig.zon, bindings/zig/src and
    // LICENSE — ten files, zero schemas — so a fetched package could not
    // validate anything. What is here now, and why:
    //
    //   bindings/zig         the library, the conformance runner, its script,
    //                        and the binding README. src/spec_schema/ holds
    //                        the twenty-one schemas the library @embedFiles,
    //                        so validation needs no files on disk at all.
    //   spec                 the normative specification and spec/schema/, so
    //                        a consumer can read what they validate against,
    //                        point CAUSALONTOLOGY_SPEC at it, and let the
    //                        runner re-check the compiled-in copies
    //                        byte-for-byte.
    //   conformance/vectors  the 137 frozen vectors, so the fetched package
    //                        is self-verifying: run
    //                        bindings/zig/run_conformance.sh inside the
    //                        fetched copy and it proves the bytes you
    //                        received, never a checkout.
    //   LICENSE, NOTICE      the attribution the licence requires,
    //                        travelling with the code.
    .paths = .{
        "build.zig",
        "build.zig.zon",
        "bindings/zig",
        "spec",
        "conformance/vectors",
        "LICENSE",
        "NOTICE",
    },
}
